# 13. QUARTER 4
## ACT Review, Exam & Postsecondary Application
### April 5 – June 11

> **Restructured 2026-08-25.** All new ACT content instruction ends at the close of Quarter 3. Quarter 4 opens with two full review weeks spanning all four ACT sections, then the exam itself, then shifts entirely to postsecondary-application content (Weeks 33-39), none of which requires completion before the exam. Exact placement of Weeks 30-32 should be confirmed once the real spring ACT date is set; the goal is for Weeks 30-31 to sit immediately before test day and Week 32 to contain the exam itself, not a fixed calendar position.

---

## Week 30: Integrated ACT Review I — Math & Science/Data

Mixed practice involving:

- Number & Quantity
- Algebra
- Functions
- Geometry
- Statistics & Probability
- Data & Scientific Reasoning
- Integrating Essential Skills
- Modeling

Students complete a full-length ACT Math practice section and a full-length ACT Science practice section, then receive targeted practice based on their own skill gaps.

Dedicated new Math and Science instruction ended at the close of Quarter 3. This week is retrieval and targeted practice only, not new content.

---

## Week 31: Integrated ACT Review II — Reading & English

Mixed practice involving:

- Reading (main idea, evidence, inference, efficient reading)
- English (sentence structure, grammar, usage, punctuation, organization, tone)

Students complete a full-length ACT Reading practice section and a full-length ACT English practice section, then receive targeted practice based on their own skill gaps.

Students identify, across all four ACT sections:

- strongest domain;
- most improved domain;
- highest-priority domain for the final days before the exam;
- recurring error type.

This week is retrieval and targeted practice only, not new content.

